              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Topping"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "nutmeg",
              "amount": 0.25,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": "grated",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "Topping"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix flour, salt, oil, and water into a smooth, firm dough. Knead for 3 minutes. Cover and rest for 10 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat oven to 240C (or as hot as it goes). Put 2 large baking trays in to heat up."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Gently soften the sliced onions in a dry pan over medium heat for 5 minutes. They should be barely cooked."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Divide the dough in half. Roll each piece on a floured surface into a thin oval or rectangle, as thin as you can manage."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Season the creme fraiche with pepper and nutmeg. Spread a thin layer over each dough base, leaving a 1cm border."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Scatter onions and lardons evenly over the top."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slide onto the hot baking trays. Bake for 8-10 minutes until the edges are golden and blistered and the lardons are cooked. Cut into pieces and serve immediately."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Base is soft and pale instead of crisp",
              "cause": "Oven not hot enough or baking tray was cold when loaded",
              "fix": "Preheat trays in the oven for at least 20 minutes before loading and use the highest oven setting"
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Dough tears when rolling",
              "cause": "Not rested enough or dough too dry",
              "fix": "Cover and rest for a further 10 minutes and add a splash more water if it feels stiff"
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Too much liquid pooled on the base from the onions",
              "cause": "Onions were raw and released moisture during baking",
              "fix": "Soften onions in a pan for 5 minutes first to remove excess water"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tarte flambee comes from Alsace, the region in northeast France that borders Germany and shares much of its food culture with it. The dish is also called Flammkuchen in German. It was traditionally baked at the end of a bread-baking session when the stone oven was at its hottest. Today it is sold by the slice from market stalls and dedicated restaurants throughout Alsace and the neighbouring German regions."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
